## Givens (Evidence)
- evidence_3: Peak traffic shows bursts up to 10x average for sub-second windows; sustained over-rate is rare.

## Lemmas (Propositions)
- proposition_4: A single global token-bucket at 1000 req/sec capped at 10000 burst protects the API.
- proposition_13: A 60-second sliding-window log per user-id (max 6000 entries) with 100 req/sec ceiling.

## Theorems (Resolutions)
- resolution_6: In addition to the global bucket, enforce a per-client-IP cap of 100 req/sec.

